---
import Layout from "@layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "@components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "@components/Footer.astro";
import Hr from "@components/Hr.astro";
import Socials from "@components/Socials.astro";
import { SOCIALS } from "@config";

const socialCount = SOCIALS.filter(social => social.active).length;
---

<Layout>
  <Header />
  <main id="main-content">
    <section id="hero">
      <h1>BACKEND | CLOUD ENGINEER Ebury | May 2022 - Present</h1>
      <h2>ENGINEER LEVEL 2 March 2024 - Present</h2>
      <p>
        In this position my work has pivoted, allowing me to work in the
        development and set up of core foundations to enable myself and peers to
        ship faster.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Conceived and deployed tools for improving the development workflow
          and CI/CD pipeline in GitHub actions which decreased time to market by
          20%.
        </li>
        <li>
          Created and established reverse proxy capabilities to allow for
          authenticated communications to hit the team’s services within GCP.
        </li>
        <li>
          Contributed to enabling authentication flows from GCP to AWS and vice
          versa.
        </li>
        <li>
          Crafted a webhook engine, a middleware framework for our APIs and a
          wrapper for a better deloper experience using GCP services.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Other duties at this role include leading projects to completion,
        identifying pain points in the development process, onboarding and
        mentoring of new team members and introducing code quality standards
        that help the team meet deadlines and KPIs.
      </p>
      <h2>ENGINEER LEVEL 1 March 2023 - March 2024</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Assisted in the designing and implementing of a critical service for
          contacting and gathering information on clients which resulted in a
          better client experience and an increase in productivity of the
          operations team by 50%.
        </li>
        <li>
          Led the refactor of key services to make them more reliable resulting
          in 30% fewer errors and a performance improvement of 20% using
          event-driven design and highly available services principles.
        </li>
        <li>
          Helped improve the debugging capabilities of the team by enhacing the
          monitoring, logging and telemetry of the services.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        My main responsibilities at this role were making key contributions to
        core projects of the team and participating in technical discussions.
      </p>
      <h2>ASSOCIATE May 2022 - March 2023</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Developed a tool for managing user accesses for the company’s CLM
          platform.
        </li>
        <li>
          Implemented a tool for performing bulk changes in core platforms of
          the company making the application support team more efficient by 40%.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        {
          // only display if at least one social link is enabled
          socialCount > 0 && (
            <div class="social-wrapper">
              <div class="social-links">Social Links:</div>
              <Socials />
            </div>
          )
        }
      </p>
      <Hr />
      <section>
        <p>testing</p>
      </section>
    </section>
    <Footer />
  </main>

  <style>
    /* ===== Hero Section ===== */
    #hero {
      @apply pb-6 pt-8;
    }
    #hero h1 {
      @apply my-4 inline-block text-3xl font-bold sm:my-8 sm:text-5xl;
    }
    #hero ul {
      list-style: disc;
      padding-left: 20px;
      margin-bottom: 1em;
    }
    #hero .rss-link {
      @apply mb-6;
    }
    #hero .rss-icon {
      @apply mb-2 h-6 w-6 scale-110 fill-skin-accent sm:mb-3 sm:scale-125;
    }
    #hero p {
      @apply my-2;
    }
    .social-wrapper {
      @apply mt-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center;
    }
    .social-links {
      @apply mb-1 mr-2 whitespace-nowrap sm:mb-0;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
